      "pronunciation_easy": "TAA-wleh la-___, law sa-MAHT",
      "qa": "Blank takes number + 'person' (شخص), and the noun changes with the number: لشخص واحد (1), لشخصين (dual, 2), لتلات/لأربع أشخاص (3-10, plural). See examples. Waiters may simply hear the number with fingers."
    },
    {
      "id": "menu_please",
      "target": "المنيو، لو سمحت.",
      "pronunciation_easy": "il-MEN-yoo, law sa-MAHT",
      "qa": "منيو is the everyday word; formal قائمة الطعام appears in print."
    },
    {
      "id": "allergic_to",
      "target": "عندي حساسية من ___.",
      "pronunciation_easy": "AN-dee ha-saa-SEE-yeh min ___",
      "qa": "ALLERGY. Literal: 'I have an allergy from ___' (= I'm allergic to ___). حساسية على ___ is also heard. Blank takes the allergen with the article (المكسرات, البيض). Gender-neutral."
    },
    {
      "id": "vegetarian",
      "target": "أنا نباتي.",
      "pronunciation_easy": "ANA na-BAA-tee",
      "qa": "Masculine form (file convention: masculine speaker/listener). Female speaker: أنا نباتية (na-baa-TEE-yeh). Literal: 'I am vegetarian'. Note: some people assume chicken/fish are fine; add ما باكل لحمة ولا جاج (I don't eat meat or chicken) if needed."
    },
    {
      "id": "without",
      "target": "بدون ___، لو سمحت.",
      "pronunciation_easy": "bi-DOON ___, law sa-MAHT",
      "qa": "ALLERGY/DIET. Literal: 'Without ___, please.' Blank takes the noun with no article (بدون لحمة, بدون حليب). بلا (BA-la) ___ is a common alternative."
    },
    {
      "id": "to_go",
      "target": "سفري، لو سمحت.",
      "pronunciation_easy": "SAF-ree, law sa-MAHT",
      "qa": "سفري ('for travel') is the standard takeaway word in Jordan/Palestine/Syria; in Lebanon 'take away' (in English) is common too."
    },
    {
      "id": "for_here",
      "target": "هون، لو سمحت.",
      "pronunciation_easy": "hoon, law sa-MAHT",
